{
  "title": "Washizu: Enma no Touhai",
  "description": "Official spin-off of Nobuyuki Fukumoto's manga Akagi.\n\nDuring the Second World War, Washizu Iwao, then a Senior Superintendent in the Special Higher Police (Tokko), was the first to predict Japan's defeat in the Pacific War due to his incredible foresight. Resigning from the Tokko entirely on his own, he escaped severe punishment as a war criminal...\n\nSo arrived the Showa 20s (late 1940s)...... Amassing funds through high-stakes mahjong against the GHQ occupying Japan, Washizu founded the management consulting firm \"Kyousei.\" Becoming an advisor to numerous corporations and acting as a pipeline between the government and business, he steadily established his position in the underworld...\n\nBehold the dawn of the Monster of the Showa Era. The bloody youth of the man destined to clash with the legendary Akagi...!",
  "artist": "Keiichirou Hara",
  "author": "Keiichirou Hara, Nobuyuki Fukumoto",
  "cover": "https://mangadex.org/covers/01e6296c-9c0f-4329-8854-036aec11595b/1ab0ff92-71cd-4a5d-b8b2-094140c8471a.jpg",
